Drop the maintenance script's reference check: its synchronous reclaim unlinks every path,
whether or not another row names it too (MEMNG-1167).

The probes that must turn red are the `sync` halves of the tier-path cases: another row's rendition
or print path naming this row's derived tier or print profile loses that file, and the reverse
order (MEMNG-1190) loses the owner's tier when the naming row goes first. Everything else in
the module drives the app's reclaim (no_reclaim_path_refcount.patch) and stays green.

